      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we start by simplifying each fraction separately using the technique of multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator.\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\):\n\nThe conjugate of \\(3 - 5i\\) is \\(3 + 5i\\).\n\nSo, multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate gives us:\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{9 + 25} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{34}.\n\\]\n\nExpanding the numerator:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(i^2 = -1\\), this becomes:\n\\[\n9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, the fraction \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\) simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\):\n\nThe conjugate of \\(3 + 5i\\) is \\(3 - 5i\\).\n\nSo, multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate gives us:\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{9 + 25} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{34}.\n\\]\n\nExpanding the numerator:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(i^2 = -1\\), this becomes:\n\\[\n9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nSo, the fraction \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\) simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nAdding the simplified fractions, we get:\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) + \\left(-\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) = \\left(-\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) = -\\frac{16}{17} + 0i = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the problem is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\n\\]",
