      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we start by finding a common denominator for the two fractions.\n\nThe common denominator of \\( (3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) \\) and \\( (3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) \\) is the same as the denominator \\( (3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) \\). This expression can be expanded using the difference of squares:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2\n\\]\n\nSince \\( i^2 = -1 \\), we have \\( 25i^2 = 25(-1) = -25 \\). So, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n9 - (-25) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nSo the denominator is \\( 34 \\). Now we can rewrite the original expression with this common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{34} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{34} = \\frac{3 + 5i + 3 - 5i}{34} = \\frac{9}{34}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified value of the expression is \\( \\frac{9}{34} \\).",
