      "text": "To simplify the given expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we'll follow a structured approach. \n\n### Step 1: Rationalize the denominators\nFirst, let us rationalize the denominators of each fraction by multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the respective denominator. The conjugate of a complex number \\(a + bi\\) is \\(a - bi\\).\n\nFor the first fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}\n\\]\nSimplify the numerator and denominator separately:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 5i^2 + 3 \\cdot 5i = 9 + 25 + 15i = 34 + 15i\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\nSo, the first fraction becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{34 + 15i}{34}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, for the second fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}\n\\]\nSimplify the numerator and denominator separately:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 + (-5i)^2 - 3 \\cdot 5i = 9 + 25 - 15i = 34 - 15i\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\nSo, the second fraction becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{34 - 15i}{34}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Combine the simplified fractions\nNow, we add the simplified fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{34 + 15i}{34} + \\frac{34 - 15i}{34}\n\\]\n\nSince the denominators are the same, we can combine the numerators:\n\\[\n\\frac{(34 + 15i) + (34 - 15i)}{34}\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n34 + 15i + 34 - 15i = 68\n\\]\nThus, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{68}{34}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Simplify the final fraction\nFinally, we simplify \\(\\frac{68}{34}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{68}{34} = \\frac{34 \\times 2}{34} = 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the final simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
